==Czech==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|cs}} {{recons|jaro|lang=sla-pro}}, {{recons|jarъ|lang=sla-pro}}, {{recons|jarь|lang=sla-pro}}, {{recons|jara|lang=sla-pro}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|cs}} {{recons|yōro-|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|yeh₁ro-||year, spring|lang=ine-pro}}, {{recons|yeh₁r-|lang=ine-pro}}. Cognate with {{etyl|en|-}} {{term|year}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|Jahr||year|lang=de}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{term|hora|hōra|hour, time, season|lang=la}}, Ancient Greek {{term|ὥρα||year, season|tr=hōra|lang=grc}}.<ref>{{R:Rejzek 2007}}</ref><ref>{{R:Machek 1968}}</ref>

